# The trade/equity logs are append-only: every scheduled run may add
# one new row at the end. Crypto and stocks now write to their own
# separate files (logs/*_crypto.csv vs logs/*_stocks.csv - see
# live_trade.py's --log-suffix), specifically so two different
# workflows committing at nearly the same moment never touch the same
# file at all. merge=union stays on all of them anyway, as a second
# layer: two commits to the SAME file (e.g. two overlapping runs of one
# workflow, or a manual local run using the same file) still hit the
# same underlying git behavior - two independent appends at the same
# end-of-file position look like a conflict to git's default merge,
# even though they don't actually overlap. Confirmed live on 2026-07-28:
# this produced a DETERMINISTIC rebase conflict that failed identically
# on every retry (not a timing race - retrying the exact same rebase
# can never resolve a real content conflict). `merge=union` tells git to
# just keep both sides' added lines instead of flagging a conflict -
# verified locally that this resolves the exact reproduced conflict
# cleanly, preserving both rows in order.
logs/trade_log_crypto.csv merge=union
logs/trade_log_stocks.csv merge=union
logs/equity_log_crypto.csv merge=union
logs/equity_log_stocks.csv merge=union
